by combining our funds with lower-cost debt. Projects that fail
to meet timing projections will increase the developer&#146;s
overall cost of funds because the developer will be carrying
debt and incurring interest for a longer period than
anticipated. Conversely, a developer whose projects sell out
ahead of schedule may benefit from a lower overall cost of funds.
