<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: #000000; background: #ffffff;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Increased liquidity needs could result in the liquidation of
loans to raise cash, thereby reducing the number and amount of
loans outstanding and the resultant earnings realized. We do not
intend to incur indebtedness; however, we may secure lines of
credit to bridge any cash needs when other sources of cash are
insufficient to meet our obligations.
</DIV>

