<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: #000000; background: #ffffff;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
A limited partner investing in us may be unable to sell any of
his units by reason of the nonexistence of any active trading
market for the units. In the event that units are sold, however,
the selling investor will realize gain or loss equal to the
difference between the gross sale price or proceeds received
from sale and the investor&#146;s adjusted tax basis in his
units. Assuming the investor is not a &#147;dealer&#148; with
respect to such units and has held the units for more than
