<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: #000000; background: #ffffff;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
In addition to the substantial understatement penalty described
above, the Internal Revenue Code also imposes a 20% penalty on
any portion of an underpayment of tax attributable to
(1)&nbsp;any substantial valuation misstatement, defined
generally as a situation where the value or adjusted basis of a
property claimed on a return is 200% or more of the correct
value or adjusted basis, or (2)&nbsp;negligence, defined as any
failure to make a reasonable attempt to comply with the Internal
Revenue Code, or a careless, reckless or intentional disregard
of federal income tax rules or regulations.
